<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36773" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pŏdălīrĭus</span></b> ,
		ii, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ποδαλείριος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Son of Æsculapius</i>, <i>a
				celebrated physician</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. Tr. 5,
				6, 11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. A. A. 2,
			735</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A Trojan who followed Æneas to Italy</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Verg.
				A. 12, 304</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A Roman surname</i>: C. PETRONIVS PODALIRIVS,
			Inscr. Amaduzzi Anecd. Litter. t. l. p. 463.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
